DISPUTE PACK: INV-2026-009876 (wholesale customer CUS-000031)
Contents: 1 sales order, 2 delivery notes, 1 price list extract, 1 email thread

== 1. SALES ORDER ORD-2026-045678 (placed 22 August) ==
Product: Linen duvet set, double, 12,000 units
Unit price on the order acknowledgement: £36.50 (price list PL-WS-2026-07, valid to 31 August)
Order value at that price: £438,000
Requested delivery: 5 September, delivery terms DAP customer DC

== 2. DELIVERY NOTES ==
DN-2026-031120 (3 September): 7,200 units received, signed clean
DN-2026-031188 (5 September): 4,440 units received, signed with note "2 pallets of 180 units not on vehicle, driver confirms short-loaded"
Total received: 11,640 units. Units invoiced but never delivered: 360.

== 3. INVOICE INV-2026-009876 (dated 8 September) ==
12,000 units at £40.00 = £480,000
Price used: PL-WS-2026-09 (effective 1 September), not the price list on the order acknowledgement.
Customer is withholding the whole £480,000 pending resolution.

== 4. PRICE LIST EXTRACT ==
PL-WS-2026-07 (to 31 August): Linen duvet set double £36.50
PL-WS-2026-09 (from 1 September): Linen duvet set double £40.00
Clause 4.2 of the trading terms: orders acknowledged before a price change are invoiced at the acknowledged price.

== 5. EMAIL THREAD ==
28 August, our sales manager to customer buyer: "Prices go up in September; I expect to confirm £38.00 on this order but need sign-off."
29 August, customer buyer: "Please confirm in writing; our PO is at £36.50."
No written confirmation of £38.00 was sent.
10 September, customer accounts payable: "Invoice rejected: price is not the agreed £36.50 and 360 units were never delivered. Please issue a corrected invoice."
12 September, our credit control: "Invoice stands as issued, please pay by 8 October."
